From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sigivb72-netizen <vergilx63@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:54:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] podot: editor: in-process game runs and iPadOS editor
 adaptations

- EditorRun/EditorNode: when instances run in-process, the editor saves,
  shuts down, the game runs in the same process, and the editor reopens
  (with the same scenes) and shows the game output in the Output dock.
- Reuse the Android mobile-editor adaptations on Apple embedded platforms
  (touch actions panel, virtual keyboard spacer in the script editor, no
  external file manager/terminal/FBX2glTF, Game tab without embedding,
  Mobile renderer by default, compact main menu).
- Save on focus loss by default on iPadOS (apps can be killed anytime).
- Use the system document picker for opening files/folders from the
  filesystem on iPadOS (reaches iCloud Drive, external drives, ...).
- Project manager: warn before opening a project that likely exceeds the
  device memory or free storage (ProjectDeviceLimits).
- Handle low-memory warnings: drop cached previews and warn the user.
- Apple hardware keyboards use the macOS key conventions (Cmd/Option).
